# Root .dockerignore — applies to any build using the repo root as context
# (apps/api, apps/web). Mirrors .gitignore plus repo-root-only exclusions
# that aren't needed inside an image build.
#
# IMPORTANT: unlike .gitignore, Docker's ignore matcher does NOT treat a
# bare `name/` pattern as "at any depth" — that needs an explicit `**/`
# prefix. Without it, nested dirs like apps/web/node_modules slip through
# `COPY . .` and silently shadow what `npm ci` just installed inside the
# container (bit us once: a Windows-built node_modules leaking in broke
# `next build` with an `exec: node.exe: not found` error).

**/.git/
**/.github/

**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/.turbo/
**/coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.uv/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/htmlcov/

**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/

**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Not needed at build time for the TS apps.
docs/
wiki/
openspec/
graphify-out/
n8n/
infra/db/
.claude/
.cursor/
.husky/
